('R1.4','Addressed by qualification and sensitivity','Sections4.2,4.4,5; pp.8,10,12; Table2','The184 historical ties include130 joint failures. We report these with46 G0-higher and70 E0-higher pairs rather than treating zeros as equal oracle quality. E0 NI is conditional on that pipeline, the shifted-rank estimand and an unvalidated working margin; E1 does not inherit it.'),
('R1.5','Open: practical margin remains unvalidated','Section3.4; Discussion and Threats; pp.6,12--13','The five-point margin is an author-selected working tolerance informed by literature context. We cannot establish that AgoneTest or the cited literature validates five points as a practically acceptable degradation. We state this limitation and do not claim stakeholder validation or new E1 NI.'),
('R1.6','Partially addressed: interpretation narrowed','Sections2.1,3.5,4.2; pp.3,7--8','The44.5% value is a published average, not a known population median. The source aggregation denominator is inconsistent and observation-level uncertainty is unavailable. RQ1 remains a comparison against a fixed threshold, not a formal two-study replication test. Original observations and statistics are preserved.'),
('R1.7','Open: no completed repeated-run evaluation','Discussion and Threats; pp.12--13','A complete within-class repeated-run evaluation is not available. The manuscript retains the single-run limitation and does not quantify run-to-run variance. Repository resampling, technical retries and configuration changes are not repeated-run evidence.'),
('R1.8','Addressed through pipeline qualification; integration limitations remain','Sections3.3,3.5,4.3,4.6; pp.5--7,9--12; Tables4,6','Historical Maven-only build counts are51/260 G0 and158/260 E0; historical Gradle counts are10/40 and0/40. E1 has19 Gradle process passes,11 failures and10 unknowns. Compilation, test execution, measurement and missing integration support remain separate; the headline comparison is pipeline-specific.'),
('R1.9','Addressed','Sections3.3,4.1,4.3; pp.5,8--9','The two GPT prewarm failures occurred before API generation. They remain in the historical300-slot pipeline denominator and receive conventional strict zeros, but are not called model-generation failures.'),
('R1.10','Partially addressed: pre-pilot analytical lock unverified','Sections3.1--3.2,3.4,6; pp.3--6,12--13','We distinguish recorded decisions before merging pilot60 with240 from an unverified analytical lock before inspecting all pilot outcomes. The minimum n≥60 rule is described as recorded, not prospectively prespecified; pilot observations remain included and the timing limitation is explicit.'),
('R1.11','Partially addressed; raw E0 provenance remains limited','Sections3.4,4.5--4.6; pp.6,10--11','The common reducer uses KILLED/all focal source-file+package rows; mutant TIMED_OUT is included only in the denominator. Valid raw reports reverify61 G0 and221 E1 scores. G0 mutant counts have median14,IQR6--31,range1--47; E1 median17,IQR8--33,range1--68. These are different cohorts. E0 implementation and archived metrics are preserved, but remaining shared-workspace reports cannot independently certify E0 per-class denominators. Class294 illustrates a genuine observed0/44, distinct from policy zeros.'),
('R1.12','Paired analysis added and claims narrowed; empirical gaps disclosed','Abstract; Sections4.4--7; pp.1,10--13','The revision provides fixed49 comparisons and assertion-enabled E1 sensitivity. It limits historical NI toE0 and does not claim that E1 is complete, equivalent or non-inferior across300 classes.'),
('R2.1','Partially addressed; not fully resolved','Sections3.3--3.5,4.5--4.6; pp.5--7,10--12','E1 uses assertion generation(MUTATION), scaffolding and EvoSuite runtime while retaining the stated BRANCH/search/archive/classloader profile. It is not represented as every EvoSuite default. The300-key ledger contains221 valid PIT observations,58 conventional pipeline failures and21 unresolved end-to-end scores. Within30 completion cases,12 lack measurements; two whole-process timeouts receive policy zeros while ten provider cases remain unknown. The extension cannot support a completed full300 E1 NI claim. Configuration and additional post-outcome integration support are disclosed.'),
('R2.2','Maven-only alternative addressed; Gradle recovery partial','Sections4.3,4.6; pp.9--12','The260-class historical Maven sensitivity remains. E1 Maven has249 determinate scores and11 unknowns, with G0−E1 mean gap−21.40pp, repository CI[−27.37,−15.66]. E1 Gradle has30 determinate scores/40slots, gap−22.66pp, CI[−53.10,10.00] across only3 available repositories. Ten missing-task cases are unknown, not generated-test compile failures.'),
('R2.3','Historical300 and fixed49 addressed; E1 full300 incomplete','Sections4.2,4.4--4.6; pp.8,10--12; Tables2,5','Historical300 and fixed49 are reported separately. E1 has279 determinate end-to-end pairs: G0/E1 means12.75/34.28%, difference−21.53pp, CI[−27.78,−15.55]. Keeping21 unknowns in[0,100] gives full300 G0−E1 bounds[−27.03,−20.03]. These are missingness bounds, not CI or a new NI test. The41 observed E1 zeros and58 conventional zeros are not conflated.'),
('R2.4','Addressed','Abstract; Section4.2 and Discussion; pp.1,8,12; Table2','The abstract retains the historical+4.84pp mean gap,46/70/184 directions and marginal A12=0.443. A12 compares cross-arm combinations; it differs from paired wins and from a rank effect on margin-shifted differences. Historical class-bootstrap intervals are labeled separately from repository sensitivity.'),
('R2.5','Open: no completed repeated-run evaluation','Sections5--6; pp.12--13','No completed within-class repeated evaluation is reported. Single-run limitations remain, and no unfinished repeated observations enter the results. Repository bootstrap cannot estimate within-arm generation variance.'),
('R2.6','Addressed as exploratory repository sensitivity','Sections3.5,4.4--4.6; pp.6--7,10--12','Whole-repository resampling preserves pairs and all sampled classes within a repository:20,000 draws,seed20261023,class-weighted mean. Historical300 uses30 repositories,fixed49 uses15,and determinateE1/279 uses28. An independent reducer reproduces the principal intervals. Conditional intervals do not solve nonrandom missingness, few Gradle clusters or post-outcome policy selection.'),
('R2.7','Addressed','Abstract; Section4.2 and Conclusion; pp.1,8,13; Table2','The20.33%(61/300) GPT process-build rate is foregrounded as8.27pp below the28.6% reference; Wilson CI[16.17,25.25]%. GPT values and cohorts61/45/300 remain unchanged. Cross-study pipeline differences still limit causal attribution.'),
('R2.minor','Addressed with evidence qualification','Section4.3/Table4 and Section4.6/Table6; pp.9,11','Table4 includes all historical stage counts. Table6 reports separate E1 generation, compilation-artifact, native-test, PIT and process-gate indicators. These overlapping indicators are not added as an exclusive failure taxonomy. E1 has222 gate passes,58 failures,20 unknowns; the58 are not all compile failures. Six valid PIT reports accompany native suites that are not fully passing.'),
('R2.path','Partially addressed overall','Sections4--7; pp.8--13','The revision adds fixed49,E1 with explicit missingness bounds,Maven sensitivity,clustering,mean/rank divergence and the GPT replication shortfall. Full E1 measurement coverage,run-to-run variance,practical margin validation and budget equivalence remain unresolved.'),
('R3.1','Additional configuration evaluated; incomplete scope retained','Sections3.5,4.5--4.6; pp.6--7,10--12','Assertions/scaffolding/runtime are enabled inE1, with other nondefault options and integration amendments stated. E1 is an incomplete pipeline sensitivity, not a controlled default-EvoSuite ranking.'),
('R3.2','Open: resource constraints documented, not equalized','Sections3.3,3.5,5; pp.5--7,12','GPT has one2048-token capped call; EvoSuite has60-second search with separate command/measurement caps. We do not claim equal compute,cost or wall-clock budgets.'),
('R3.3','Addressed as exploratory sensitivity','Sections3.5,4.4--4.6; pp.6--7,10--12','Repository resampling supplements the retained historical class-level analyses. Available-cohort inference and missingness bounds are explicitly different summaries.'),
('R3.4','Partially addressed: diagnostics and integration support disclosed','Sections3.3,3.5,4.3,4.6,6; pp.5--7,9--13','Arm-scoped historical logs distinguish symptoms and integration failures. E1 amendments restore prepared inputs or adjust test/measurement support with provenance, retaining suites when already generated. Business source and generated assertions are not repaired. G0 did not receive matching support; keeping its observations fixed alone does not establish environmental fairness. One class3 diagnostic selection is disclosed with original-outcome sensitivity.'),
